      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the balance thing, but i'm a bit worried about the vibe of the museum. if we lead with all the tragedy and the \"human costs\" right at the start, won't that just make the whole \"spirit of discovery\" theme feel forced or even wrong? wouldn't it be more accurate to say that the progress and the expansion were just inevitable historical forces that happened regardless of the conflict?",
